# fxmind — auto Task

For implementation requests read `.fxmind/modes/task.md`. Questions/reviews remain read-only unless changes are requested. "Analyze and fix" authorizes implementation; respect decisions already made and user stop.

Use relevant preloaded memories or fxmind_query; confirm with current source. Missing coverage → fxmind_search in the affected directory, or permitted native search. Use MCP for gates and available domain operations. Missing MCP blocks gated edits, not read-only diagnosis.

Quick/full controls effort, not quality. Trivial means a known tiny one-file change with no new behavior; UI and risky tasks use A/B. Gates: start → A → B → implement + diff review → V with actual evidence → C. Keep sessionId; claim task files for parallel edits. Never write gate/session JSON.

Read `.fxmind/modes/task-verify.md` before UI edits and before V. UI requires browser interactions, visual inspection and an existing screenshot/trace. Build alone cannot verify UI. Failed/blocked checks leave V incomplete, and edits after V require re-verification.

Keep constants/helpers/files only when they add concrete value. Match local conventions; preserve security checks. Record gate notes once instead of duplicating ceremony in chat. User-facing replies are short and direct — outcome first, no long text.
